<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- DEVICE (sideload) entitlements, trimmed for free-Apple-ID personal-team signing.

     Removed vs upstream:
       - com.apple.security.application-groups: App Groups are a team-scoped entitlement and Apple does
         not issue them to free personal teams. The GainsWidget target that consumed the group has been
         removed from project.yml; WidgetSharedStore falls back to UserDefaults.standard (see
         Sources/Shared/WidgetShared.swift, `UserDefaults(suiteName:) ?? .standard`), so nothing breaks.
       - keychain-access-groups: KeychainStore passes a nil access group on device
         (Sources/Services/KeychainStore.swift, the #if targetEnvironment(simulator) split), so iOS uses
         the app's automatic default group. Declaring a group here would only create a signing mismatch
         for Sideloadly's free provisioning profile. Whoop tokens still persist normally.

     Kept: HealthKit, so weight imports from Apple Health. If the free personal team refuses to
     provision it, delete the two lines below and rebuild; weight entry then becomes manual. -->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.healthkit</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
